{"title":"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chord</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> to a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of the radius. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of the larger of the two regions into which the chord divides the circle to the smaller can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf239aa19e8c60b0df8111e522478cf1d00e5843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\pi+b\\sqrt{c}}{d\\pi-e\\sqrt{f}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9789be024235f74358e909a3c347a12acf7a19fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d, e,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a>, and neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility\" title=\"Divisibility\"> divisible</a> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> of any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a>. Find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Remainder\" title=\"Remainder\">remainder</a> when the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c84f7ee6833ea13782445dfd147c97a98e03f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcdef$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2004_AIME_II_Problem_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/75/2004_AIME_II_Problem_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"304\" height=\"304\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">length</a> of the radius of the circle.  A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a> is formed by half of the chord, half of the radius (since the chord <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bisect\" title=\"Bisect\">bisects</a> it), and the radius. Thus, it is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a>, and the area of two such triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfaab9dc0188bb0f860faa3faa2c94e303d9092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{r}{2} \\cdot \\frac{r\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{r^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"178\" height=\"41\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Central_angle\" title=\"Central angle\">central angle</a> which contains the entire chord is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef1faafd786afdf7065f73648cfa1f7665eab69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\cdot 2 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degree\" title=\"Degree\">degrees</a>, so the area of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sector\" title=\"Sector\">sector</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b06490a33fd4f5d66085b14bdc92194a8d54659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}r^2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"39\" height=\"37\" />; the rest of the area of the circle is then equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/0039d42f45effd3c874ecd483e6115c6d5708f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}r^2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"39\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The smaller area cut off by the chord is equal to the area of the sector minus the area of the triangle. The larger area is equal to the area of the circle not within the sector and the area of the triangle. Thus, the desired ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2538763ae7195e280837d10916b9e27a1261ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{2}{3}r^2\\pi + \\frac{r^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}}{\\frac{1}{3}r^2\\pi - \\frac{r^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}} =  \\frac{8\\pi + 3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi - 3\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"204\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/3691eb250c16af3609f028531170d9cd879007a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcdef = 2^53^4 = 2592 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{592}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II\" title=\"2004 AIME II\">2004 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016212147\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 182/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1775/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3450/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.645      1 -total\n 58.30%    7.372      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.99%    5.056 